{
  "summary": "This experiment tested transformer-based aggregation in the multiprofile RNA-only setting (scvi_n200 encoder) as a single-variable comparison against the avgpool configuration (llm_summary_004), yielding a validation accuracy of 0.653 (F1 0.628) versus 0.650 (F1 0.628) for avgpool. The ~0.3-point accuracy gain and near-identical F1 suggest that, under this configuration, transformer aggregation captures at most a marginal improvement over simple average pooling, indicating that the aggregation strategy is unlikely to be a dominant remaining bottleneck within the multiprofile regime. It remains uncertain whether this small difference is statistically meaningful, whether other aggregation architectures or transformer hyperparameter tuning could yield larger gains, or whether further improvements are more likely to come from encoder exploration (e.g., scgpt) or multimodal fusion."
}

